{#- The commonplace book, on a page of its own because the owner asked for one: the quotations get a place of
    their own (owner ruling, 2026-09-21; record kept privately). Since 2026-09-26 it reads as a reading room
    (external review 3 §24; controller decision C2 under owner ruling 18; record kept privately): each line,
    then its source on one compact line, then one note, in his order -- Snape first -- and with no date
    gutter, because the page is deliberately not a chronology; the year is in the source line. The margin
    rule stays as the page's quiet spine, from the title's tick to "Last updated", with no tick of its own
    for an entry (decided by render in both themes; the reasons are in style.css, "Reading"). -#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}

{% block main %}

    <section id="quotes" aria-labelledby="quotes-h">
      <h1 id="quotes-h" class="inset">{{ page.heading }}</h1>
{% if site.get("quotes_intro") %}
      <p class="page-intro inset">{{ m.nb(site.quotes_intro) }}</p>
{% endif %}
{% if site.get("quotes") %}
      <ul class="reading inset" role="list">
        {{ m.quote_entries(site.quotes)|trim }}
      </ul>
{% endif %}
    </section>

{% endblock %}
